The Sandal Path: My Mission to the Red Team
I am not just a student; I am a dedicated researcher on a mission to master the art of offensive security. This blog serves as the live documentation of my progress, from the first command line to the most complex exploit.

How it Started: The Battlefield Classroom
My journey didn't begin in a typical way. During my recent military reserve duty, I found a unique window of opportunity. In the gaps between operations, 
I decided to turn my dream of becoming a hacker into a reality. With a laptop and unwavering focus, I started my journey on TryHackMe, spending countless hours mastering networking and offensive fundamentals while still in uniform.

Formal Education: The CyberProAI Foundation
Upon returning to civilian life, I committed to formalizing my knowledge. I am currently a student in the intensive Cybersecurity Practitioner program at CyberProAI. 
This 600-hour academic program is providing me with a solid foundation in:
Infrastructure Mastery: Windows, Linux, and Advanced Networking.
Defensive Operations: Understanding SIEM, SOC, and EDR from the ground up.
Offensive Security: Ethical Hacking and Network Security principles.
Self-Driven Research: Going Beyond the Classroom
I believe that true mastery comes from independent exploration. Parallel to my studies, I am building my "attacker mindset" through rigorous labs:
Linux Internals: Developing deep CLI fluency through Bandit (OverTheWire) and pwn.college.
Infrastructure & AD: Hands-on practice in breaking Active Directory environments and machine exploitation.
Web Security: Deep-diving into HTTP/1.1 and modern web vulnerabilities (currently conquering Natas).

Why "SandalGod"?
It represents my philosophy: Stay comfortable, think clearly, and dig deep. I may be learning and "breaking" systems in sandals, but my commitment to becoming a world-class Red Teamer is absolute.

Follow my journey as I document every lesson learned, every machine pwned, and every step closer to the mission.
